<!--
  companions-gate.dtd : the one gate every bypass runs through.

  The matrix command lets the user choose permission mode bypass for
  companions, audit runners and scala-matrix companions so long CI legs
  never stall on a prompt nobody can answer. Two tiers: leashed, where
  bypass removes the PROMPTS and the guard still refuses every writing
  tool, chain, redirect, background field and substitution; and
  unlocked, where named writing tools are admitted inside a named
  scope, ordered by the owner at grant time. The tree is compared
  before and after under both tiers, and an undisclosed delta fails
  the run under both tiers.

  Findings ride the .nt schematic read in one gulp, reverse as the
  prior gate.yml run showed; under unlocked the companion may persist
  them itself inside its scope, and the runner still stamps the record.
-->

<!-- ===== THE ROLES ===== -->
<!-- One grant per role a bypass may carry. Three, named, never open. -->
<!ENTITY % cg.role "(companion|audit-runner|scala-companion)">
<!ENTITY CG.roles "companion|audit-runner|scala-companion">
<!ENTITY CG.roles.count "3">
<!-- role | what it may run | what persists its findings -->
<!ENTITY CG.role.companion      "read engines of this repository and reading git verbs, one wrapper call at a time|the runner tees stdout to the scratchpad">
<!ENTITY CG.role.audit-runner   "the phase diff, the tree, and the scorer|checker/companion-audit.sh writes the record with the run stamp">
<!ENTITY CG.role.scala-companion "chain tokens under --no-gate plus read engines, scored by sigil headings and the close line|the runner writes artifacts/research/DATE-scala-findings.nt, or the companion itself under unlocked inside its scope">

<!-- ===== THE TIERS ===== -->
<!-- Leashed is the default; unlocked is ordered per grant, never ambient. -->
<!ENTITY % cg.tier "(leashed|unlocked)">
<!ENTITY CG.tiers "leashed|unlocked">
<!ENTITY CG.tier.leashed  "prompts removed, guard refusals absolute|the tier every grant carries unless unlocked is ordered">
<!ENTITY CG.tier.unlocked "named writing tools admitted inside a named scope|ordered per grant with tools, paths and ceiling written down first">

<!-- ===== WHAT BYPASS DOES AND DOES NOT TOUCH ===== -->
<!ENTITY CG.bypass.does "remove permission prompts so unattended legs never stall|named model, effort and thinking envs ride the nested session">
<!ENTITY CG.bypass.does-not-leashed "admit a writing tool|admit a chain, pipe, redirect, background field or substitution|admit stdin readers|admit commands without their own ceiling|skip the tree compare">
<!ENTITY CG.bypass.unlocked-admits "named writing tools inside the named scope only|the tools, the paths and the ceiling are written in the grant before launch">
<!ENTITY CG.bypass.unlocked-keeps "no background field and no spawned agent under any tier|stdin closed on every command|a ceiling on every command|the tree compare with disclosure">
<!ENTITY CG.ceiling "portable, node lib/ceiling.mjs where timeout is absent|stdin closed on every command, exit 124 reads UNAUDITED per LAW.COMPANION.5">

<!-- ===== ELEMENTS ===== -->
<!ELEMENT gate_grant (grant+)>
<!ELEMENT grant (#PCDATA)>
<!ATTLIST grant
          role       %cg.role;  #REQUIRED
          tier       %cg.tier;  "leashed"
          permission (bypass|default) #REQUIRED
          tools      CDATA #IMPLIED
          scope      CDATA #IMPLIED
          model      CDATA #REQUIRED
          effort     (low|medium|high|xhigh|max) #REQUIRED
          ceiling    CDATA #REQUIRED>

<!-- ===== LAWS ===== -->
<!ENTITY LAW.CG.1 "A bypass grant names one of CG.roles, CG.roles.count of them; a grant naming any other role, or none, is refused before the session launches.">
<!ENTITY LAW.CG.2 "Under tier leashed, bypass removes prompts and nothing else: every refusal of the guard (writing tools, chains, redirects, background fields, substitutions, stdin readers, ceiling-less commands) holds exactly as under default, and a session that met one is scored as refused, never as passed.">
<!ENTITY LAW.CG.3 "The tree, HEAD, porcelain status and ignored files minus the runner's own stream are compared before and after the session under both tiers; any delta the runner did not write and the grant did not name is the companion's breach, disclosed in the scope or scored fail.">
<!ENTITY LAW.CG.4 "Under tier leashed the companion never persists: findings leave through stdout and the runner writes them, stamped with the run; under unlocked the companion may persist inside its scope and the runner still stamps the record; findings ride the .nt schematic read in one gulp, reverse.">
<!ENTITY LAW.CG.5 "The nested session carries the model, effort and thinking the matrix chose; the budget stays unset and the hard zero stays --thinking disabled per LAW.MX.5, because a bypassed session with no thinking dial is a session that cannot be steered.">
<!ENTITY LAW.CG.6 "The grant, its role, tier, model, effort and ceiling are rendered as one grant element before the session starts; a session that ran without a rendered grant is unaudited, never scored.">
<!ENTITY LAW.CG.7 "Tier unlocked is ordered, never ambient: the grant names the tools, the scope paths and the ceiling first, and the runner launches the nested session without the denying guard for those names alone; permission mode bypass by itself never lifts the hook, so a file edited without this law behind it is still a breach under LAW.CG.3.">
<!ENTITY LAW.CG.8 "Unlocked keeps every stall law: no background field, no spawned agent, stdin closed, a ceiling on every command; unlocked changes what may be WRITTEN, never what may run away, and a runaway under unlocked fails the run exactly as under leashed.">
<!ENTITY LAW.CG.9 "The suite holds this file: every new refusal and admission carries a control that trips it on purpose, or the gate that cannot prove its gate ships red by declaration; the runner unlock arm and its controls ride the same release as this law, never a later one.">
